04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature’s controller doesn’t control an Island, that creature is an illegal target. Whether that player controls an Island is checked both when Seasinger’s ability is activated and when it resolves. However, targeting restrictions aren’t checked continually while a spell or ability is on the stack.","oracle_id":"13745b92-1e30-4075-9733-5d00da11408c","published_at":"2007-09-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Whether you control Seasinger is checked continually, starting when the ability is activated. If, before the ability resolves, there’s any point at which you don’t control Seasinger, the ability has no effect — even if you control Seasinger again by the time the ability resolves. The same is true regarding whether Seasinger remains tapped.","oracle_id":"13745b92-1e30-4075-9733-5d00da11408c","published_at":"2007-09-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This has basic land types, but it isn't a basic land. Things that affect basic lands don't affect it. Things that affect basic land types do.","oracle_id":"74b7fe23-5d3a-4092-8d78-7c0eba8f6f73","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This has the mana abilities associated with both of its basic land types.","oracle_id":"74b7fe23-5d3a-4092-8d78-7c0eba8f6f73","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
